":"green_checks_failed divides by every synced run, including runs whose commit GitHub did not know (checks_conclusion null) and runs whose checks were pending, so they count as 'did not fail'. pull_request_found likewise counts a missing commit as 'no pull request'. Absent evidence must be left out, not counted as a negative.","fix_commit":"8e772d7a2b87393af6c8524c3ddaf707ab7ce632","id":"F001","line":609,"path":"agentic_preflight/report.py","response_note":"Shares now exclude pending and unknown-commit runs and report them as excluded.","severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Divide the failed share by synced runs with settled checks and the PR-found share by synced runs whose commit GitHub knew; report the excluded runs.","title":"Hosted failed and PR-found shares count runs without evidence as negatives","unit":"U0007"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"A live read-only check showed GET /commits/{sha}/pulls returns [] for the heads of PRs 263 and 168, which were closed without merging. pr is then null, so abandoned pull requests disappear and the merged share is overstated.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F002","line":311,"path":"agentic_preflight/hosted.py","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"When the commit has no associated pull request, read /pulls?state=all&head={owner}:{branch} and use the pull request whose head is the commit.","title":"Pull requests closed without merging are never found","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"Summaries are regenerated only after the fetch loop. If the process stops after some hosted.json files were written, the next sync treats those runs as synced and skips them, so their summary.json and mirror rows never gain the outcome until a manual rebuild.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":551,"path":"agentic_preflight/hosted.py","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Treat a synced run whose summary.json hosted.fetched_at differs from its hosted.json as stale and regenerate it without a request.","title":"Summaries stay stale after an interrupted sync","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"Every GhError stops the loop. Runs are fetched newest first, so a commit that always returns a 5xx or an unreadable answer is retried first on each run and older runs are never synced.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F004","line":457,"path":"agentic_preflight/hosted.py","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Record http_error and invalid_response in data.errors and continue; stop only for auth, rate limit, network, 403, 404, and write failures.","title":"One commit that keeps failing blocks every older run","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"run.get('conclusion') in a frozenset raises TypeError for an unhashable value such as a list. It escapes the loop as internal_error, losing data.synced for runs already written.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F005","line":262,"path":"agentic_preflight/hosted.py","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Compare telemetry._str(run.get('conclusion')) and convert unexpected parse errors into a per-commit invalid_response.","title":"A non-text check conclusion crashes the reduction","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The code counts only failure, cancelled, and timed_out as failures, but the table names only skipped and neutral as non-failures, so a reader can assume action_required or stale fail the checks.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F006","line":144,"path":"docs/local-telemetry.md","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"List the three failure conclusions and give action_required and stale as examples of non-failures.","title":"The success row does not say which conclusions are failures","unit":"U0018"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"When --run names a run whose record cannot be read, eligible is 0 and next.instruction says the run is not a DONE run with a pushed commit, which is wrong. Also data.gh_found stays null when nothing is selected, while commands.md says it tells whether PATH has gh.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F007","line":143,"path":"agentic_preflight/cli_telemetry.py","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Skip that message when the record is unreadable, and set gh_found before any early return.","title":"--run on an unreadable record says the run is not DONE","unit":"U0004"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The playbook says to run sync-hosted one time per clone, and synced runs are skipped, so outcomes read while checks were pending or a pull request was open never update. The playbook never mentions --refresh.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F008","line":198,"path":"skill/reference/playbooks.md","response_note":"Fixed by repair commit 8e772d7, which is recorded under F001; the CLI takes one in-place repair commit per submission, so this note records the fix.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Tell the agent to add --refresh --limit 10 only when the user wants recent runs read again.","title":"Playbook gives no way to update pending outcomes","unit":"U0024"},{"action":"no_op","code_owned":false,"detail":"Pagination stops after 10 pages of 100 check runs, and checks.total stores the number read. A commit with more than 1,000 check runs is not realistic for this tool's users, so the cap stays as a bound on requests.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F009","line":278,"path":"agentic_preflight/hosted.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"open","suggestion":"None.","title":"Check runs past ten pages are not read","unit":"U0005"},{"action":"no_op","code_owned":false,"detail":"summary_stale compares hosted.json fetched_at with the summary's. If fetched_at is not text, the summary carries null, the values never match, and each sync regenerates that one summary without a request. Only a hand-edited file can reach this, and the cost is one local summary write.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F010","line":411,"path":"agentic_preflight/hosted.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"open","suggestion":"None; --refresh rewrites the file.","title":"A hand-edited hosted.json without a text fetched_at is regenerated on every sync","unit":"U0005"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"21c58f623c41cafe2d41d1b1ce6860f9d0445713","config_sha256":"83d0937adfa85eafbcd13121104a92d2f1e6f4878a5484d0b93bee0bde1d63de","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"b9d460b91c13784b3ee0f9048a25084307a3700e3bcf14dc14e11cff6c8e65a9","excluded_files":[],"executor":"in_harness","grounding_sha256":"fce41841342e57ebd56edb65a7a5a7fdd4925dc19efb1c553ff58222ac2680b8","head_tree_sha":"fbb1167ee6496350d46b1976d9a33f3a5c07deb3","intent_sha256":"b8cb0d1cfe372a8c0383d9b73fbcb89d6625eb1524fa3d3fad793fcf5503e1a3","version":2},"